    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (78.38) and **Jacob Wilson** (64.35). **Gunnar Henderson** remains our premier start against Dean Kremer; his 14% dynamic platoon boost and top-of-the-order designation drive his elite status. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor and a manageable matchup against Freddy Peralta, whose 4.29 xERA suggests volatility that **Jacob Wilson** is well-positioned to exploit from the two-hole. **Kyle Tucker** also provides a high floor (64.04), serving as a core component of our offense despite a lukewarm platoon outlook.\n\nThe most difficult decision at the margins involved **Wade Meckler** (38.79), who narrowly missed the starting cut. While **Wade Meckler** offers an enticing leadoff role, his L/L platoon disadvantage against MacKenzie Gore significantly depressed his efficiency score below our standard threshold. We are monitoring the weather in three venues\u2014specifically for **Drake Baldwin**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Dominic Smith**\u2014where a 31% rain risk could compress our total game volume. While **Andy Pages** (59.46) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (59.41) hover near the strong threshold, their combination of projected lineup slots and favorable park adjustments confirms their inclusion in the final lineup. We will continue to monitor the status of **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Luis Lara** as depth pieces, though today\u2019s lineup prioritizes the current efficiency projections over bench versatility.",
